## Third-party content

The MIT grant above covers this project's own source, configuration, and
documentation. The material below is authored by others and carries its own
terms. Nothing here restricts the MIT grant on the rest of the project; it
records what the MIT grant does *not* reach.

### Corpus (`idle_hours/assets/`)

The excerpts in `idle_hours/assets/candidates-attributed.jsonl` and
`idle_hours/assets/quote_database.jsonl` are mined from works sourced via
Project Gutenberg (https://www.gutenberg.org/). The individual works are in the
public domain in the United States; other jurisdictions may vary, and a
redistributor outside the US should confirm the status of the works they ship.
The compilation, cleaning, scoring, and bucketing of those excerpts is this
project's own work and is covered by the MIT license above.

"Project Gutenberg" is a trademark of the Project Gutenberg Literary Archive
Foundation. This project is not affiliated with or endorsed by the Foundation,
and the mined excerpts carry none of the Project Gutenberg licence header, so
the trademark terms attaching to a full PG ebook do not attach here.

### Bundled typefaces (`idle_hours/fonts/`)

Each family lives in its own subdirectory alongside its upstream license text.
All are under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1, except the two noted
below, which are under the Apache License 2.0:

- `idle_hours/fonts/special-elite/` — Special Elite, Apache-2.0
  (`special-elite/LICENSE.txt`)
- `idle_hours/fonts/permanent-marker/` — Permanent Marker, Apache-2.0
  (`permanent-marker/LICENSE.txt`)

Every other subdirectory of `idle_hours/fonts/` ships an `OFL.txt` covering the
face beside it, and `idle_hours/fonts/OFL.txt` covers the Playfair Display files
at the top level (upstream: https://github.com/clauseggers/Playfair-Display).

Both licences require their text to travel with the work, which is why the
license file sits in each family's directory rather than being summarised here;
a face added without one is a licensing defect, not a cosmetic omission.

### Images (`idle_hours/assets/`)

`anna_atkins_cyanotype.png`, `daguerreotype_plate.png`, `grimdark_gunmetal.png`,
`letter_aged_paper.png`, `goodnight.png`, `logo.svg`, `preview.png`,
`contact-sheet.png`, and everything under `previews/` are this project's own
work, generated by the committed scripts under `scripts/` or by the renderer
itself, and are covered by the MIT grant. In particular the plates rendered in a
historical idiom (the Atkins-style cyanotype, the daguerreotype landscape) are
original works in that idiom rather than reproductions of any specific
photograph.

### Runtime dependencies

Dependencies are installed from PyPI rather than vendored, so none of their code
is redistributed here. All are permissively licensed: Pillow (MIT-CMU) at
runtime, plus `inky` (MIT) and `gpiozero` (BSD-3-Clause) under the optional
`[pi]` extra.
